    <div class="faq">
      <div class="faq-item reveal"><button class="faq-q">Is Shopify good for SEO? <span class="pm"></span></button><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes. Shopify offers solid foundations: editable titles and metas, 301 redirects, an automatic sitemap, canonicals by default, HTTPS. The problem almost always comes down to those fields being empty or poorly filled.</p></div></div>
      <div class="faq-item reveal"><button class="faq-q">Can you change URLs on Shopify? <span class="pm"></span></button><div class="faq-a"><p>Partly. You can edit a product's or collection's "handle", but not the enforced prefixes (/products/, /collections/). Your SEO architecture is built inside those constraints.</p></div></div>
      <div class="faq-item reveal"><button class="faq-q">Do you need an SEO app on Shopify? <span class="pm"></span></button><div class="faq-a"><p>Not necessarily. Many levers are handled natively. Stacking apps weighs down the theme and can hurt speed. The priority is the content of your collections and product pages.</p></div></div>
      <div class="faq-item reveal"><button class="faq-q">Why does a reseller outrank my Shopify listing? <span class="pm"></span></button><div class="faq-a"><p>Because their page is often better filled out (content, signals, internal links) than yours. It's a capture problem, not a platform problem. The Diagnostic quantifies it and sets the priorities.</p></div></div>
      <div class="faq-item reveal"><button class="faq-q">How long before SEO results on Shopify? <span class="pm"></span></button><div class="faq-a"><p>Winning back your branded SERP is faster (a few weeks) than conquering a contested category query (several months). The Diagnostic puts the quick wins first.</p></div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec" style="padding-top:0">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="links-more reveal">
